From 1f5665e66eb3b4b4d6bad962a039cdbb6fc03958 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xu Qianhui <xuqianhui1001@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:49:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input-method-relay: Fix NULL deref in keyboard grab destroy
 handler

wlroots 0.20.0 changed the signal emission convention and passes NULL as
the signal data when emitting wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2::events.destroy,
see wlroots commit 06275103 ("input-method-v2: Destroy keyboard grab
before input method").

phoc still assumed the old convention where the keyboard grab was passed
as signal data and dereferenced it unconditionally, so any input method
tearing down its keyboard grab crashed the compositor with a SIGSEGV:

  Thread 1 "phoc" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.
  #0  handle_im_keyboard_grab_destroy ()
  #1  wl_signal_emit_mutable ()
  #2  wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2_destroy ()
  #3  wl_client_destroy ()

The fault address is NULL + offsetof(struct wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2,
keyboard), i.e. 0x10 on aarch64.

Note that only one input method can be connected to a seat. When a second
one connects phoc sends it "unavailable", but the grab teardown path is
the same, so the crash was easy to hit on a device where both an
on-screen keyboard and a regular input method engine were present: the
compositor died and the whole session got restarted.

The grab is still attached to the input method while the signal is
emitted, so look it up there when data is NULL. This also keeps working
with wlroots versions that still pass the grab as data.

Signed-off-by: Xu Qianhui <xuqianhui1001@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
 src/input-method-relay.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/input-method-relay.c b/src/input-method-relay.c
index a9829b2..a7ac07c 100644
--- a/src/input-method-relay.c
+++ b/src/input-method-relay.c
@@ -118,9 +118,15 @@ handle_im_keyboard_grab_destroy (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
     wl_container_of (listener, relay, input_method_keyboard_grab_destroy);
   struct wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2 *keyboard_grab = data;
 
+  /* wlroots emits this signal with the grab as data up to 0.19 and with NULL
+   * from 0.20 on (see wlroots commit 06275103). The grab is still attached to
+   * the input method when the signal is emitted so get it from there. */
+  if (keyboard_grab == NULL && relay->input_method != NULL)
+    keyboard_grab = relay->input_method->keyboard_grab;
+
   wl_list_remove (&relay->input_method_keyboard_grab_destroy.link);
 
-  if (keyboard_grab->keyboard) {
+  if (keyboard_grab && keyboard_grab->keyboard) {
     /* send modifier state to original client */
     wlr_seat_keyboard_notify_modifiers (keyboard_grab->input_method->seat,
                                         &keyboard_grab->keyboard->modifiers);
-- 
